# Summary — Sections 4 through 10

## 4. `OperationLogger` — the log-level contract

**Three methods, three levels:**

| Method | Level | Sentry | Email |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Success(msg)` | Information | No | No |
| `Warning(msg)` | Warning | No | No |
| `Error(msg, ex)` / `Error(msg)` | Error | **Yes** | **Yes** |

- Removed `Fail` and `Reject` entirely.
- `Error` is the **only** method that reaches Sentry.
- Added `_disposed` guard so double-dispose (from `using` + explicit call) is a no-op.

**Sentry config in `Program.cs`:**
```csharp
options.MinimumEventLevel = LogLevel.Error;
options.MinimumBreadcrumbLevel = LogLevel.Information;
```

Business rejections stay in Serilog only. Real bugs page you.

---

## 5. `ExceptionHandlingMiddleware` — rewritten

- `op.Fail(...)` → `op.Error(...)` for 5xx, `op.Warning(...)` for 4xx.
- `OperationCanceledException` handled first — **only** when `context.RequestAborted.IsCancellationRequested` (true client disconnect). HttpClient timeouts no longer get swallowed.
- `TimeoutException` and `TaskCanceledException` → **504 Gateway Timeout** (was 408) so DB/provider timeouts reach Sentry.
- `Response.HasStarted` uses `Warning` — not a bug.

**Final status map:**

| Exception | Status | Sentry |
|---|---|---|
| Client disconnect | — | No |
| `ArgumentException` / `InvalidOperationException` / `ValidationException` | 400 | No |
| `UnauthorizedAccessException` | 401 | No |
| `KeyNotFoundException` | 404 | No |
| `DbUpdateException` | 409 | No |
| `DbException` | 503 | Yes |
| `TimeoutException` / `TaskCanceledException` | 504 | Yes |
| `NotImplementedException` | 501 | Yes |
| Everything else | 500 | Yes |

---

## 6. `UnitOfWork` — auto-rollback on scope dispose

- `IUnitOfWork` now extends `IAsyncDisposable`.
- `DisposeAsync` rolls back any uncommitted transaction when the request scope ends.
- `_transaction = null` set **before** `CommitAsync` / `RollbackAsync` to prevent double-dispose if commit itself throws.

**New helper:**

```csharp
await using var tx = await _unitOfWork.BeginAtomicAsync(ct);
// ... work
await tx.CommitAsync(ct);   // not called → auto rollback
```

This is the piece that lets every handler drop its try/catch.

---

## 7. `NotificationQueue` — `TryEnqueue` pattern

**The rule:**
- Handler: **never** has try/catch.
- `NotificationQueue.TryEnqueue`: owns the try/catch, logs via `op.Error`, returns normally.
- Middleware: only sees failures that mean the request itself failed.

**Why:** if enqueue throws after the DB write committed, the middleware returns 500 and the client thinks the whole operation failed — even though the money moved.

**`NotificationQueue.cs` now:**
- Wraps every `_backgroundJobClient.Enqueue<...>(...)` in `TryEnqueue`.
- Injects `ILogger<NotificationQueue>`.
- On failure: `op.Error("Failed to enqueue notification job.", ex)` → Sentry + email, handler keeps going.
- Worker-side retry already handled by `[AutomaticRetry(Attempts = 3)]` on `BackgroundNotificationJob`.

---

## 8. `BreakWalletCommand` — refactored

- **Zero try/catch.**
- `await using var tx = await _unitOfWork.BeginAtomicAsync(ct)` replaces manual `BeginTransactionAsync` + rollback.
- Business rejections **throw** instead of returning 400/404:
  - `throw new KeyNotFoundException("Wallet not found.")` → 404
  - `throw new InvalidOperationException("...")` → 400
- PIN challenge failure → `op.Warning(...)` (business, no Sentry).
- Notifications called directly — no try/catch, no Hangfire coupling in `Application`.

---

## 9. Tests

**New test files (13):**

`GetAllWalletsQueryTests` (15) · `GetReleasesQueryTests` (16) · `GetRenewalEventsQueryTests` (12) · `GetRenewalPolicyQueryTests` (12) · `GetWalletActivitiesQueryTests` (17) · `GetWalletAnalyticsQueryTests` (22) · `GetWalletBankAccountQueryTests` (8) · `GetWalletCategoriesQueryTests` (9) · `WalletDetailsQueryTests` (25) · `GetWalletSchedulePreviewQueryTests` (18) · `ListWalletTemplatesQueryTests` (19) · `SchedulePreviewQueryTests` (10) · `GetWalletPayoutsQueryTests` (20) · `DatabaseSeederTests` (17)

**Base test infrastructure:**
- `SqliteStringArrayConverter` added to `BaseTest` — Postgres `text[]` columns now round-trip as JSON on SQLite (fixes `WalletTemplate.Tags`).

**Recurring lessons the tests caught:**
- Every entity seed must populate every non-nullable column (`Payout.Reference`, `Transaction.Reference`, `RenewalEvent.TransactionId`, …).
- Moq matches reference types by reference, not value → use `It.Is<T>(x => x.Id == id)` for entities EF materialized.
- `(string, object)[]` tuple shape needs explicit `+ (object)` casts when passed to `OperationLogger.Start`.

---

## 10. CI — `build-check.yml`

Added `verify-connectivity` job:
- Runs after `test`.
- Only on push/dispatch (no PRs — secrets aren't available to forks).
- Verifies Postgres (`SELECT 1`) and Redis (`PING`) against production credentials using `tools/Mova.HealthCheck`.
- `promote-to-production` now `needs: [test, verify-connectivity]` — no deploy if either fails.
- Two new repo secrets: `POSTGRES_CONNECTION_STRING`, `REDIS_CONNECTION_STRING`.